The ResenderHandler builds a replacement dictionary from ALL ChatMessageDict fields for {{variable}} substitution in job.messagePrefix/job.messageSuffix (internal/bot/common/handlers/resender.py:426-444):

```python
replaceDict: Dict[str, str] = {}
for k, v in message.items():             # ALL ChatMessageDict fields
    replaceDict[k] = str(v)
if message["metadata"]:
    metadataDict = json.loads(message["metadata"])
    for k, v in metadataDict.items():
        replaceDict[f"metadata.{k}"] = str(v)
        if isinstance(v, dict):
            # One level of nested flattening: metadata.{k}.{k2}
            replaceDict.update({f"metadata.{k}.{k2}": str(v2) for k2, v2 in v.items()})
```

Available template variables (from ChatMessageDict at internal/database/models.py:129-184): chat_id, message_id, date, user_id, reply_id (NOT reply_to_message_id), thread_id, root_message_id, message_text, message_type, message_category, quote_text, media_id, created_at, metadata, markup, media_group_id, username, full_name (username/full_name from the User table), plus NotRequired model_id and score on search rows. Also any metadata.* sub-keys (e.g. metadata.bot_username, metadata.forwardedFrom.type) and one nested level metadata.{k}.{k2} for dict values.

Note: the message text body itself (messageText) is NOT template-expanded — only prefix/suffix are.

When adding observability/diagnostic logging that serializes pydantic objects in `BasicOpenAIModel._executeChatCompletion` (`lib/ai/providers/basic_openai_provider.py`, the empty-output block ~lines 364-406), the "observability only" contract requires that the diagnostic MUST NOT change behavior — no assignment to `status`, `resText`, `retMessage`, or any local flowing into the returned `_OpenAICallOutcome`; no early return/raise inside the block.

Specifically, bare `.model_dump()` calls on token-detail objects (`completion_tokens_details`, `prompt_tokens_details`) MUST be wrapped in `try/except Exception:` with a `str(<obj>)` fallback. Reason: a pydantic serializer failure on a vendor's subclass would propagate out of `_executeChatCompletion`, masking the original SUCCESSFUL API outcome — turning an observability probe into a behavior change. This mirrors the existing `responseDump` pattern at the same site (try/except around serialization).

Canonical shape per detail object (applies to both `completionTokensDetailsDump` and `promptTokensDetailsDump`):
```python
if completionTokensDetails is None:
    completionTokensDetailsDump = "None"
elif hasattr(completionTokensDetails, "model_dump"):
    try:
        completionTokensDetailsDump = repr(completionTokensDetails.model_dump())
    except Exception:
